- When suggesting code or solutions, remember to check docs/memory.md for project context
- Suggest updating docs/memory.md when important project information needs to be remembered
- Only implement one feature at a time
- Before suggesting commits, remind about formatting and error checking
- Keep track of bugs in docs/bugs.md but don't update bug statuses unless user confirms a fix
- Do not suggest committing files to git when fixing bugs, unless user confirms the issue is fixed
- Do not suggest running dev server if it appears to be already running

- This project uses docs/memory.md to store important project information
- The project tracks bugs in docs/bugs.md
- Code quality and documentation are emphasized before making commits
  
### Memory files
- docs/memory.md
- docs/bugs.md

### Workflow Reminders
- Format code with `npm run format`
- Lint code with `npm run lint`
- make sure code is formatted, checked for errors, all docs are updated, and results are committed to git before starting a new feature
- Make sure code is formatted, checked for errors, and all docs are updated before making a commit
